==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|oblacion}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|oblātiō||offering}}, from {{term|offero|offerō|I offer, present}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/əʊˈbleɪʃən/|/ɒˈbleɪʃən/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/oʊˈbleɪʃən/|/ɑːˈbleɪʃən/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-oblation.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|eɪʃən|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[offering]] of [[worship]], [[thanks]] etc. to a [[deity]].
#* '''1786''', {{w|William Beckford}}, ''Vathek; an Arabian Tale'':
#*: whatever she judged proper for the '''oblation''' of the approaching night.
# A [[deed]] or [[gift]] offered [[charitably]].

